<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kinzig (Main)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kinzig is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> that flows south-west between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vogelsberg">Vogelsberg</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spessart">Spessart</a> through Gelnhausen to join the Main at Hanau. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> built his imperial palace on an island in the river at Gelnhausen. Its valley carried the old road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulda">Fulda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kinzig-main.jpg" alt="Kinzig (Main)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MdE · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kinzig_Bulau_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
